      "writtenOn": "2023-01-11T00:41:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am a little hesitant, as the communication protocol between the USB host computer and the HyperDebug board is still being developed.  It is possible that we want to switch away from text console commands, and instead use a binary protocol via USB.  It is certain that some extensions is going to be required to support the various modes of Quad-SPI.  In short, I would like to be able to make modifications to the convention without worrying about other boards possibly having started to rely on what I have added.",
      "parentUuid": "37c314c6_68a4893f",
      "revId": "63ff8a02df6f7e0776bd693a1ac58a0684c961fc",
